> I'll play the odd elvish wiz, but never really altar camp for
> books...Just...if i find them, wahey! More than once i've found an
> uncursed book early game, read it, and  BAM!!! DYWYPI?! (damn lvl 7
> spells >.>)

I've learned that unless I'm a wizard reading any spellbook that is not
blessed carries a risk.  In the early game quaffing from a fountain is a
big risk.  In the mid game reading a not-blessed spellbook is that level
of risk.

I do altar camp for books in some games.  Even as a valk at times.  If I
have a way to create monsters I may well altar camp until I wear it out
to get the other benefits.  Getting spellbooks is one of the goals doing
that as a wizard, but it doesn't suck as a side effect for other
classes.  At worst it's a way to be confused if you're not in a speed
game.

> Getting crowned still isn't in my list of "i must do this!!!!",
> however, some people seem to think it's the end of the world!

There's an entire spectrum between atheist conduct and altar camping
until you max out at AC -127 and you have tons of books.

I also tend to keep a stash near an altar as I explore down and when I
return to that level if I can check to see if it's safe to pray I do. 
But if I altar camp for a while I often take getting crowned as the
game's way of telling me that it's time to go back to exploring down and
stop camping.  I've played games at plenty of different points along
that spectrum.


